      "side": 1,
      "message": "If that\u0027s the case, why don\u0027t we leave CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_DERATE_PCT undefined in config.h and break a build or print a warning if it\u0027s not defined?\n\n    #include \"board.h\"\n    ...\n    #ifndef CONFIG_CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_DERATE_PCT\n    #ifdef CONFIG_SYSTEM_UNLOCKED\n    #WARN CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_DERATE_PCT not defined.\n    #else\n    #ERROR CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_DERATE_PCT or board_set_charge_limit must be defined.\n    #endif\n    #endif\n\nYou can probably find a smarter way to handle both CHARGER_INPUT_CURRENT_DERATE_PCT or board_set_charge_limit.",
